  "name": "BACTERIAL PNEUMONIA PANEL PCR",
  "code": "2274",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Test Method(s)</strong><br><strong>BACTERIAL PNEUMONIAE PANEL-Multiplex DNA Polymerase Chain Reaction.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clinical Utility :</strong><br>It is a rapid, sensitive &amp; specific test for diagnosing lower respiratory tract infections by three most common<br>respiratory pathogens i.e. Mycoplasma pneumoniae, Streptococcus pneumoniae and Chlamydia pneumoniae<br>With no suitable method to culture, this is the best test to identify Chlamydia pneumoniae and Mycoplasma<br>pneumoniae directly in clinical specimens<br>It is also a useful test to document eradication of the pathogen after appropriate treatment.</p>\n<p>Presence of target specific bands indicates either Mycoplasma pneumoniae, Streptococcus pneumoniae or Chlamydia&nbsp;pneumoniae in the given specimen.&nbsp;No target specific amplification indicates absence of Mycoplasma pneumoniae, Chlamydia pneumoniae, or Streptococcus&nbsp;pneumoniae in the given specimen.&nbsp;All the results should always be correlated with clinical status and history of the patient.</p>\n<p>Limitations :<br>PCR is a highly sensitive technique common reasons for paradoxical results are contamination during specimen collection,&nbsp;selection of inappropriate specimens and inherent PCR inhibitors in the specimen.</p>",
